 "A free tool for contract-holders dealing with damp and mould in Welsh rented homes.": "",
 "A month with nothing done is the point to involve your council. This is free, it does not need a solicitor, and it is the route landlords take most seriously.": "",
 "Black spotted mould in cold corners, worse in winter. You will likely be told it is your lifestyle. Check whether the extractor fans actually work and whether the windows open — if they do not, those are defects, they are cheap to fix, and they shift the argument back where it belongs.": "",
 "Built and maintained by a PCA-qualified damp and timber business. This tool is free and carries no obligation — if it tells you the fault is your landlord's, take it to your landlord.": "",
 "Councils assess housing hazards partly on who is exposed to them. A household including a child, an older person or someone with asthma or another respiratory condition raises the severity score, and that changes what the council can require your landlord to do. Never leave it out.": "",
 "DampCheck Wales | Free Damp &amp; Mould Help for Renters": "",
 "Free tool for renters in Wales. Work out what your damp or mould is, learn your landlord's duties, and write a dated report to send them.": "",
 "I reported this by phone on 3 March and again on 20 April. My daughter has asthma. The extractor fan in the bathroom has never worked.": "",
 "If the extractor fan in your bathroom or kitchen does not work, say so explicitly in writing. It is a concrete defect, it is cheap to fix, and it undercuts the lifestyle argument immediately.": "",
 "Put it in writing today if you have not already. A phone call you cannot evidence is worth very little later.": "",
 "Rust-red dust and white strands point to a fungus that travels through masonry and eats structural timber. It needs a persistent water source, so something is leaking. This is the one form of damp that gets significantly worse and more expensive the longer it is left. Report it today and use the word \"fungus\" in writing.": "",
 "Soft, dark, crumbling wood in a wet area. Contained and fixable — but the water reaching it has not been stopped, so replacing the timber alone buys about a year.": "",
 "Two months. If private, report the landlord to Rent Smart Wales. If social, your complaint should be through their process and ready for the Public Services Ombudsman for Wales.": "",
 "Two weeks with no inspection arranged is long enough to follow up. Reply to your own email so the original date stays in the thread.": "",
 "Water crossing the wall from outside through a specific fault: cracked render, failed pointing, a split downpipe, a slipped slate, a chimney flashing. It is a building repair and squarely a landlord repair. Say in your letter that it worsens after rain — that detail does a lot of work.": "",
